{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith","id":1245905,"title":"A psychic kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-14T09:00:33-07:00","id":1245905,"title":"A psychic kith","content":"Would it be overpowered to create a kith that could purchase supernatural merits and fuel them with glamour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:25:24-07:00","id":1245950,"title":"","content":"Freely? It might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:59:17-07:00","id":1245965,"title":"","content":"You could have them purchase Supernatural Merits, fuel them with Willpower (which is normal), and have the kith convert Glamour to Willpower.<br /> <br /> (2 or 3 Glamour to Willpower would be appropriate--start high and then take a Merit to make it more efficient?)<br /> <br /> Ironically since normal Willpower regain is linked to a good night's rest in mortals, the kith could link to gentle repose in some fashion (Sandman?).<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:15:29-07:00","id":1245974,"title":"","content":"Overpowered would be subjective. But it does go against the guide for creating custom Kiths where you're supposed to get a unique power rather than an advantage like the ability to buy Supernatural Merits. I would rather take a single Supernatural Merit and modify it until it was strong enough to be a Kith Trickery.<br /> <br /> This discussion begs the question, are Changelings explicitly prohibited from purchasing Supernatural Merits in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:56:44-07:00","id":1246004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1245974#post1245974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion begs the question, are Changelings explicitly prohibited from purchasing Supernatural Merits in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, right there in character creation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Step Six: Merits</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Choose 10 dots\u2019 worth of Merits. The Lost may possess any of the Merits from the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook, <b>except for those on the Supernatural Merits list</b>, Vice-Ridden, and Virtuous (since changelings do not have Virtue and Vice traits). As well, consult the extensive list of Lost-specific Merits on p. 111.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T15:08:41-07:00","id":1246073,"title":"","content":"Yeah; generally all of the major gameline splats are prohibited from getting any of those Merits. They're only for mortal characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T16:34:57-07:00","id":1246111,"title":"","content":"I don't think granting access to Mortal Supernatural Merits is appropriate for a kith blessing, but it <i>might </i>be appropriate for a Court Mantle (similar to the Coils of Zirnitra from <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>) or by being replicated through Goblin Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T16:45:50-07:00","id":1246115,"title":"","content":"How exactly does court mantle benefits work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T19:43:53-07:00","id":1246161,"title":"","content":"The underhill previews included a kith called the Grey that could use the Telepathy merit, and a few other kiths that worked sort of the same way; that is to say they would get one (usually three dot) supernatural merit that tied into their theme.<br /> <br /> You would have to rework them a bit to match up with current kiths but it's not that difficult of a port in most cases. If it's something you want to do I don't think it's going to throw &quot;balance&quot; off that much, most supernatural merits aren't that potent, and many are outclassed by contracts with similar but more powerful effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:21:10-07:00","id":1246163,"title":"","content":"Umm, aren't there already kiths with supernatural merits? Isn't there a kith with telepathy, one with clairvoyance, and another with a cures effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:39:43-07:00","id":1246168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246163#post1246163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm, aren't there already kiths with supernatural merits? Isn't there a kith with telepathy, one with clairvoyance, and another with a cures effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the final version and not outside the context of a single unified concept, setting aside the fact that those were pretty clearly not actually &quot;these kiths have these Supernatural Merits&quot; so much as &quot;these kiths have abilities mechanically similar to these Supernatural Merits.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T21:33:47-07:00","id":1246176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246168#post1246168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in the final version and not outside the context of a single unified concept, setting aside the fact that those were pretty clearly not actually &quot;these kiths have these Supernatural Merits&quot; so much as &quot;these kiths have abilities mechanically similar to these Supernatural Merits.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So Chatelain no longer has protection against supernatural powers that would cause her to make a faux pause, Grey's no longer have the three dot telepathy merit, and Oracles no longer have the ability to look into the future<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T21:52:55-07:00","id":1246179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246176#post1246176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Chatelain no longer has protection against supernatural powers that would cause her to make a faux pause,</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. They just need less successes to get an Exceptional Success on Empathy test to &quot;determine a target's true desires&quot; and they can use other character's Social Merits as if they were their own. And that's it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Grey's no longer have the three dot telepathy merit, and Oracles no longer have the ability to look into the future<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />? </div> </div> </div>An official version of Greys and Oracles in this version of CtL2e currently do not exist, so we have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:04:29-07:00","id":1246182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246179#post1246179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. They just need less successes to get an Exceptional Success on Empathy test to &quot;determine a target's true desires&quot; and they can use other character's Social Merits as if they were their own. And that's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> An official version of Greys and Oracles in this version of CtL2e currently do not exist, so we have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Grave Wrights exist? If so, how has their blessing been edited?<br /> <br /> And your description of the Chatelain kith's blessing makes me wonder how the Dear Hearts Blessing has changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:10:58-07:00","id":1246184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246182#post1246182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do Grave Wrights exist? If so, how has their blessing been edited?<br /> <br /> And your description of the Chatelain kith's blessing makes me wonder how the Dear Hearts Blessing has changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are only 12 kiths in the corebook: Artist, Bright One, Chatelaine, Gristlegrinder, Helldiver, Hunterheart, Leechfinger, Mirrorskin, Nightsinger, Notary, Playmate, and Snowskin. Helldiver and Notary, I believe, are brand new kiths to CtL period.<br /> <br /> More kiths are planned for the upcoming supplement &quot;Kith and Kin&quot;, but thus far (as far as I know) it hasn't been revealed which kiths will be in it. Nevermind which 1e kiths, or Underhill kiths will be appearing in them, if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:15:28-07:00","id":1246185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246184#post1246184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are only 12 kiths in the corebook: Artist, Bright One, Chatelaine, Gristlegrinder, Helldiver, Hunterheart, Leechfinger, Mirrorskin, Nightsinger, Notary, Playmate, and Snowskin. Helldiver and Notary, I believe, are brand new kiths to CtL period.<br /> <br /> More kiths are planned for the upcoming supplement &quot;Kith and Kin&quot;, but thus far (as far as I know) it hasn't been revealed which kiths will be in it. Nevermind which 1e kiths, or Underhill kiths will be appearing in them, if at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much have Bright Ones and Gristlegrinders blessings changed?<br /> <br /> I am also very curious about the Hell Diver. Could you give a description of it, plus its blessings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:17:58-07:00","id":1246186,"title":"","content":"More kiths are planned for the upcoming supplement &quot;Kith and Kin&quot;, but thus far (as far as I know) it hasn't been revealed which kiths will be in it. Nevermind which 1e kiths, or Underhill kiths will be appearing in them, if at all.<br /> <br /> \u200bI turned in two Kiths, Banshee and Daemonic, which I was informed were being looked over for consideration. I hope these two make it into the Kith and Kin book<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:37:59-07:00","id":1246193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246185#post1246185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much have Bright Ones and Gristlegrinders blessings changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Compared to their 1e versions or Underhill versions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am also very curious about the Hell Diver. Could you give a description of it, plus its blessings? </div> </div> </div>Ok let's see what I can do without straight up quoting the whole kith write-up...<br /> <br /> First off, kiths in general now have two mechanics associated with them: Blessings and Trickeries. Blessings are a specific Skill that, in specific circumstances, they achieve an Exceptional Success on three successes instead of the usual five successes. Trickeries are a unique power that represents the specific purpose that kith was built for by their Gentry master.<br /> <br /> Helldiver's thing is that they are explorers. That while they were in Arcadia, the Gentry would send them to either explore uncharted parts of the Hedge, but sometimes even CofD's Otherrealms. Meaning that this is one of the more crossover friendly kiths. When describing their Trickery, they even specifically call out the Shadow and Underworld as places they can go. And presumably they can go to other places like the Astral Realms or the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Their Blessing reduces the successes for an Exceptional Success when using Larceny in an Otherrealm. Their Trickery, Dive, makes them invisible and incorporeal, shifting them into &quot;Twilight&quot;. This is what allows them to travel to any of the Otherrealms, assuming that a gateway for said realm is nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:41:28-07:00","id":1246194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246193#post1246193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Compared to their 1e versions or Underhill versions?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Underhill versions<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T23:20:06-07:00","id":1246201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246194#post1246194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underhill versions</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then...the general idea of their Trickery is the same: Bright Ones still emit a bright light that can blind people, Gristlegrinders can still eat people. The mechanics behind their ability are completely different.<br /> <br /> Bright One's Trickery, Flare, unlike the Underhill version, any enemy targeted by Flare don't get a roll to resist it. If they get hit, they're hit. While they don't get the Blinded Tilt if they're hit, instead they just take a -2 on all Physical and Mental actions for one turn, and they take 1 point of bashing damage. Although if they have the Glamour to spare, they can keep using Flare each turn.<br /> <br /> For Gristlegrinders, To Serve Man, they can still make bite attacks without needing to grapple that causes lethal damage. The amount of kilograms they can devour isn't a factor here. Instead it's about devouring enemies whole (if they're a smaller Size then you). The target takes damage over time while inside the Gristlegrinder's stomach, and that they need to deal 5 lethal damage with one attack to break out.<br /> <br /> So aside from changing the actual mechanics, this version simplifies the mechanics compared to the Underhill versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T07:01:33-07:00","id":1246313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246201#post1246201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok then...the general idea of their Trickery is the same: Bright Ones still emit a bright light that can blind people, Gristlegrinders can still eat people. The mechanics behind their ability are completely different.<br /> <br /> Bright One's Trickery, Flare, unlike the Underhill version, any enemy targeted by Flare don't get a roll to resist it. If they get hit, they're hit. While they don't get the Blinded Tilt if they're hit, instead they just take a -2 on all Physical and Mental actions for one turn, and they take 1 point of bashing damage. Although if they have the Glamour to spare, they can keep using Flare each turn.<br /> <br /> For Gristlegrinders, To Serve Man, they can still make bite attacks without needing to grapple that causes lethal damage. The amount of kilograms they can devour isn't a factor here. Instead it's about devouring enemies whole (if they're a smaller Size then you). The target takes damage over time while inside the Gristlegrinder's stomach, and that they need to deal 5 lethal damage with one attack to break out.<br /> <br /> So aside from changing the actual mechanics, this version simplifies the mechanics compared to the Underhill versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Trickery for converted Greys could easily be replicating the mechanics (ask a question about the subject's mental state/thoughts) in exchange for a Glamour, for example.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Ability to buy Supernatural Merits is probably not feasible, but I could see the Trickery for a &quot;Mind-Thief&quot; Kith being that they could &quot;borrow&quot; the use of such a Merit from another by spending a Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T19:34:16-07:00","id":1246515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246313#post1246313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Trickery for converted Greys could easily be replicating the mechanics (ask a question about the subject's mental state/thoughts) in exchange for a Glamour, for example.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Ability to buy Supernatural Merits is probably not feasible, but I could see the Trickery for a &amp;quot;Mind-Thief&amp;quot; Kith being that they could &amp;quot;borrow&amp;quot; the use of such a Merit from another by spending a Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make that a resisted roll, though, and be one that you need to be aware of first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T20:07:46-07:00","id":1246522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1245905-a-psychic-kith?p=1246515#post1246515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would make that a resisted roll, though, and be one that you need to be aware of first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, as the mechanical details, but the concept is fine, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T21:09:44-07:00","id":1246531,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the power can work, though it would require characters with powers and merits that could be replicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}